      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1548775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T21:08:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`int_pin` is a phandle pointing to a `named-gpios` node. `int-pin` is a property of *chip*.yaml. `gpios` is a property of the `named-gpios` node that stores all the gpio specs. \n\nHere\u0027s an example of how they\u0027re used in the .dts:\n\n```\n\\* fragment from i2c.dts *\\\ntcpc_port0: ps8xxx@b {\n\tcompatible \u003d \"parade,ps8xxx\";\n\treg \u003d \u003c0xb\u003e;\n\tint-pin \u003d \u003c\u0026gpio_usb_c0_pd_int_odl\u003e;\n};\n\n\\* fragment from gpio.dts *\\\nnamed-gpios {\n\tcompatible \u003d \"named-gpios\";\n\n\tgpio_usb_c0_pd_int_odl: usb_c0_pd_int_odl {\n\t\tgpios \u003d \u003c\u0026gpioe 0 GPIO_INPUT\u003e;\n\t\tenum-name \u003d \"GPIO_USB_C0_PD_INT_ODL\";\n\t};\n};\n```",
      "parentUuid": "8eb00d87_47283eab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "892a25bf3af33f88b528f2aa2c824ccb04695946",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
